Close an open buffer by removing its associated fsys directory.
To ensure that success of this test isn't just down to the file
failing to open, we copy the content of the file to second file
first and make sure that worked as well.

-- config --
path: tests/data/config/with-fsys.toml
-- file-start-empty.txt --
-- file-remove-me.txt --
Testing
-- actions --
# yank from buffer 2
type: xy
# switch to buffer 1
type: :b 1\n
# paste
type: p
fsys: rm buffers/2
-- buffer-list --
1    * start-empty.txt
-- expected-windows --
1
-- expected-buffer-1 --
Testing
